    "teaching_notes": "Activate AFTER showing the infographic image of electricity use categories. Say: 'You've seen the seven categories — now let's test if you can sort these appliances correctly!' Allow the student to work independently. If they struggle with borderline items, discuss the concept of PRIMARY use. For example, a computer could arguably be used for communication or entertainment, but its PRIMARY use is categorized under 'Others'. Discuss with students why some devices might belong to multiple categories.",
    "instructions_for_student": "Drag each electrical appliance card into its correct category! Think about the PRIMARY purpose of each device. Sort all 14 appliances correctly to complete the activity!",
    "learning_objectives": [
        "Identify common electrical appliances used in Indian households and daily life",
        "Classify electrical appliances into seven major categories of electricity use",
        "Understand the PRIMARY purpose of each electrical device",
        "Reinforce understanding of how electricity serves different purposes in daily life",
        "Connect textbook knowledge (NCERT Chapter 3) with real-world Indian context"
    ],
